* stmono1.scheme
* dash translation of Stata's stmono1 graph scheme.
*
* SOURCE            : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-stmono1.scheme
*                     (resolved through its #include chain:
*                      s2color -> s1color -> s1mono -> stmono1,
*                      plus /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/style/*.style)
* STATA VERSION     : StataNow 19.5 (MP), born 12 Aug 2026
* EXTRACTED (UTC)   : 2026-09-19T16:13:55Z
* DERIVED FROM      : test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json ["stmono1"], generated by
*                     scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py.  Regenerate that fixture
*                     and re-derive this file if Stata is upgraded; the values
*                     below were last true as of the date above.
*
* Every colour is written as a RESOLVED #rrggbb hex triplet, never as a Stata
* colour name.  OptionTranslator._COLOR_MAP covers only a subset of Stata's
* colour names, and SchemeParser._color() silently substitutes its #000000
* default for any token it cannot translate -- which is how an unresolved name
* turns a whole scheme black.  Hex is self-contained and cannot be swallowed.
*
* Property categories used by dash SchemeParser:
*   color, symbol, linepattern, linewidth, intensity, gsize, graphsize,
*   symbolsize, clockdir, numstyle, yesno
*
* No property of stmono1 is null in the fixture, so nothing is omitted here.

label "Stata mono 1"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Background and region colors
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color background      #ffffff
color plotregion      #ffffff
color legend          #ffffff
color legend_line     #ffffff
color major_grid      #e0e0e0
color minor_grid      #505050
color heading         #000000
color axisline        #000000

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Per-plot color cycle (p1-p15)   [Stata: color p1 .. color p15]
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color p1      #606060
color p2      #a0a0a0
color p3      #808080
color p4      #404040
color p5      #000000
color p6      #c0c0c0
color p7      #202020
color p8      #707070
color p9      #909090
color p10     #b0b0b0
color p11     #d0d0d0
color p12     #505050
color p13     #303030
color p14     #c0c0c0
color p15     #505050

* Per-plot line color.  Stata resolves all 15 through the single directive
* "color pline"; dash has no pstub key, so the one value is spelled out p1-p15.
color p1line   #000000
color p2line   #000000
color p3line   #000000
color p4line   #000000
color p5line   #000000
color p6line   #000000
color p7line   #000000
color p8line   #000000
color p9line   #000000
color p10line  #000000
color p11line  #000000
color p12line  #000000
color p13line  #000000
color p14line  #000000
color p15line  #000000

* Per-plot bar/area fill color   [Stata: falls back to color p1 .. color p15]
color p1bar    #606060
color p2bar    #a0a0a0
color p3bar    #808080
color p4bar    #404040
color p5bar    #000000
color p6bar    #c0c0c0
color p7bar    #202020
color p8bar    #707070
color p9bar    #909090
color p10bar   #b0b0b0
color p11bar   #d0d0d0
color p12bar   #505050
color p13bar   #303030
color p14bar   #c0c0c0
color p15bar   #505050

* Per-plot marker fill color   [Stata: falls back to color p1 .. color p15]
color p1mark   #606060
color p2mark   #a0a0a0
color p3mark   #808080
color p4mark   #404040
color p5mark   #000000
color p6mark   #c0c0c0
color p7mark   #202020
color p8mark   #707070
color p9mark   #909090
color p10mark  #b0b0b0
color p11mark  #d0d0d0
color p12mark  #505050
color p13mark  #303030
color p14mark  #c0c0c0
color p15mark  #505050

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Marker symbol cycle
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbol p1     circle
symbol p2     diamond
symbol p3     square
symbol p4     triangle
symbol p5     x
symbol p6     plus
symbol p7     circle_hollow
symbol p8     diamond_hollow
symbol p9     square_hollow
symbol p10    triangle_hollow
symbol p11    smcircle
symbol p12    smdiamond
symbol p13    smsquare
symbol p14    smtriangle
symbol p15    smx

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line patterns for line/connected plots
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linepattern p1line   solid
linepattern p2line   dash
linepattern p3line   vshortdash
linepattern p4line   longdash_dot
linepattern p5line   longdash
linepattern p6line   dash_dot
linepattern p7line   dot
linepattern p8line   shortdash_dot
linepattern p9line   tight_dot
linepattern p10line  dash_dot_dot
linepattern p11line  longdash_shortdash
linepattern p12line  dash_3dot
linepattern p13line  longdash_dot_dot
linepattern p14line  shortdash_dot_dot
linepattern p15line  longdash_3dot

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line widths (Stata linewidth style names)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linewidth p           medium
linewidth major_grid  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fill intensities
* "intensity area" is not set by any Stata base scheme; stmono1 resolves it
* through the bare intensity class default, which is "full".
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
intensity p        inten80
intensity bar      full
intensity area     full

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Font sizes (Stata gsize keywords)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gsize text          medium
gsize heading       large
gsize axis_title    medsmall
gsize tick_label    medsmall
gsize note          small

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Graph dimensions, in inches (consumed by section 10)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphsize x   7.5
graphsize y   4.5

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Default marker size, legend placement, and major-grid switches
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbolsize p              small
clockdir legend_position  3
numstyle legend_cols      1
* GRID VISIBILITY.  A Stata grid belongs to an AXIS and the key is named for
* that axis's orientation, not for the direction of the lines:
*   style/axisstyle-horizontal_default.style:18  draw_major_grid <- draw_major_hgrid
*   style/axisstyle-vertical_default.style:18    draw_major_grid <- draw_major_vgrid
* The horizontal axis is x, and its major grid lines are the VERTICAL ones at
* the x ticks; the vertical axis is y, and its lines are HORIZONTAL.
* `yesno draw_major_grid' below is transcribed faithfully from Stata's file but
* is DEAD at scheme level: grep "scheme draw_major_grid" over
* /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/style/ returns nothing.  dash used to read it
* for the y axis, which is why every scheme reported "no grid" and dash drew
* both anyway.
yesno draw_major_hgrid    no
yesno draw_major_vgrid no
yesno draw_major_grid     no

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* HONEST GAP (project rule 2) -- the p#lineplot keys
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Stata does not read a plain `twoway line` plot's line from the
* `p#line` scheme keys.  It reaches the `p#lineplot` keys through two
* style files:
*   style/seriesstyle-p#line.style:5   set line    scheme p#line
*   style/linestyle-p#line.style:4-7   set width   scheme p#lineplot
*                                      set color   scheme p#lineplot
*                                      set pattern scheme p#lineplot
* So `linepattern p#lineplot` is the dash pattern of `twoway line`, while
* the `linepattern p#line` block above is what style/linestyle-p#.style
* reads -- the connecting line of `twoway connected`.  Stata documents the
* three keys in scheme_line_plots.sthlp:29-34 as the colour, thickness and
* pattern "for #th line plot".
*
* NO `color p#lineplot` OR `linepattern p#lineplot` DIRECTIVE IS WRITTEN IN
* THIS FILE, because stmono1's #include chain (s2color -> s1color -> s1mono
* -> stmono1) declares none at any level. Of all the scheme files Stata
* ships, only scheme-s2mono.scheme and scheme-s2gmanual.scheme contain a
* `lineplot` directive at all; the three occurrences in scheme-s2color.scheme
* (lines 457, 604 and 1250) are commented-out examples, not settings. There
* is therefore nothing to translate here, and a value written in would be a
* fabrication.
*
* NOTE, because it is the opposite of s2mono and easy to get backwards:
* stmono1 DOES declare a varied `linepattern p#line` cycle
* (/Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s1mono.scheme:152-166), written
* out above. That cycle belongs to `twoway connected`. It does NOT reach
* `twoway line`, which reads p#lineplot and finds none, so Stata draws every
* stmono1 line plot solid.
*
* Recorded for the reader, NOT as directives, because these are values Stata
* falls back to rather than values stmono1 writes
* (scheme_line_plots.sthlp:52-56: "If a scheme does not contain some of the
* line-plot specific entries above, then the look of those elements of line
* plots will be determined by default entries that are shared among all
* plottypes"; the shared entries are `color p#` and `linepattern p`, per
* scheme_shared_plots.sthlp:20-31):
*   linepattern p#lineplot -> linepattern p = solid
*       (/Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s2color.scheme:599)
*   color       p#lineplot -> color p#, i.e. the `color p1`..`color p15`
*       values already written above
*       (/Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s1mono.scheme:53-67)
